<section class="page-intro container"><a class="back-link" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}practice/`}>← Practice</a><span class="eyebrow">Practice / Psychotherapy</span><h1>A space to<br /><em>be heard.</em></h1><p class="lede">A collaborative space to explore what feels difficult, confusing or unfinished, at a pace that respects your needs.</p></section>
<section class="container detail-body"><div class="prose"><p>My clinical interests include emotional difficulties, relationships, grief and loss, trauma, identity, cross-cultural transitions and questions of meaning.</p><p>I am informed by existential-humanistic and feminist perspectives. Rather than fitting experience into a predetermined explanation, I value careful listening and collaborative meaning-making.</p><p>The form and pace of the work are discussed together. If you are considering starting, you are welcome to write with a brief description of what you are looking for.</p></div><aside class="detail-aside"><span class="eyebrow">Related areas</span><p>Psychotherapy · Embodiment · Movement</p><a class="text-link" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}workshops/`}>Explore workshops <span>↗</span></a></aside></section>
